[{"id":"VRCE-4-38-1","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":38,"verse":1,"english":"As Sugrīva was speaking thus with joined hands, that best of the righteous, Rāma, embraced him with his arms, and then replied,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.884,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-39-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4038001","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dc55a9978c635d9cae25b300982e42c3c867cc85f018fca9f2c459152df7220d","compact":"482b9dd905cb853884b3472baa253b30ca79e13fed8098b4f62b220b2616bef7","nasal":"0e4db43f71913d91b7f51650d29fdda97b91d07cbd8393102c9e0029753871cf"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-38-2","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":38,"verse":2,"english":"That Indra poureth down showers, is no wonder, nor that this thousand-rayed Sun dispels darkness from the sky; nor yet that, O mild one, the Moon by his rays causes the clear night. (And in a similar way), friends like you bring delight, O subduer of foes. O mild one, that 'whatever is graceful, should be harboured in you is not strange.* *The commentator in his usual way of reading between the lines, says that the sense is—That you had gathered forces for serving your friend, is not strange. O placid one, it is well. I give the sense the śloka naturally yields.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.571,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-39-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4038002","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e05e9f01d59df459f7b9517c8883e36e51071ddd199ac5f02d4c9a93fb425e5f","compact":"7692a19a953f81cbed76445a8e0fde76023ac2c832fd0b07a4faf9544bdd10b6","nasal":"896234f0e673972c60cfafec330b1f19c3d0f0057850967c4e6c1277fbcabd20"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-38-3","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":38,"verse":3,"english":"That Indra poureth down showers, is no wonder, nor that this thousand-rayed Sun dispels darkness from the sky; nor yet that, O mild one, the Moon by his rays causes the clear night. (And in a similar way), friends like you bring delight, O subduer of foes. O mild one, that 'whatever is graceful, should be harboured in you is not strange.* *The commentator in his usual way of reading between the lines, says that the sense is—That you had gathered forces for serving your friend, is not strange. O placid one, it is well. I give the sense the śloka naturally yields.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.538,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-39-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4038003","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b760ff79686a8b1982c811fe0a041e003426714b9a9ce634dbb44e6e00b2f84d","compact":"3b4d52bdf0c9cb05f4ee52ad0a8ffb1c3c3bcf43c1a312252bebb415d87ce57f","nasal":"ff127f92d389941242d910d93d16c74f739255ebb80706d7d43d304f99691858"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-38-4","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":38,"verse":4,"english":"I know, O Sugrīva, that you always speakst what is for my good.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-39-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4038004","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dfe2edac457fc975f8308c118775966b281d2f109418e6d923c183e406a9c71f","compact":"51c2320275c053b2155c92642ec1ed2c63a22500f102af6b6c0d8b118ad683a0","nasal":"51c2320275c053b2155c92642ec1ed2c63a22500f102af6b6c0d8b118ad683a0"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-38-5","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":38,"verse":5,"english":"Assisted by you, my friend, I shall in battle vanquish all my foes. You being my friend and my ally, should assist me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-39-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4038005","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6d49584b31a59099b4458fcd2f930f0c82c7508b2c95aa3054e2108796f1d074","compact":"254b6b66744989589919b33aef638604394bce643426c4f10a13be0011b6c1aa","nasal":"8db775e50e19fea898c7226f189dce3a2096b0c11ec38d9598278f74959b424a"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-38-6","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":38,"verse":6,"english":"That worst of Rākșasas has carried away Maithilī, to bring down destruction upon himself, even as Anuhlāda ravished Puloma's daughter, Sachi, deceiving her sire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.767,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-39-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4038006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c673d61ffe48128f8fd5e8a60dfd5978acb145b39454fe63c5fed8cdccab3044","compact":"42ec56a056ce416556cdbdcfb40e2385b6c0fdbc950c715deab559443f32b1b7","nasal":"e597918ad96c6efb0b3dd39d2393a1555e7b0db63f66282d711492df2a3d7f6c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-38-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":38,"verse":7,"english":"That Rāvana I will at no distant date slay with my sharpened shafts, even as that slayer of enemies, he of an hundred sacrifices-slew the haughty father of Paulomi.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-39-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4038007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"09735339b211a846f33724439435ba3f3f748cfa7a9ead866115941ed221937a","compact":"165d392a26290e31cba341ba349826e1624b3ce3f87d0eb54ed5400e308f2c5d","nasal":"165d392a26290e31cba341ba349826e1624b3ce3f87d0eb54ed5400e308f2c5d"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-38-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":38,"verse":8,"english":"Presently appeared volumes of dust, and the hot and fierce rays of the sun were hid in the sky.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-39-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4038008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1620f5250cc470f84cf6089c469ef80f79a08f02ad26ec83f6cefb3671fe819e","compact":"f1f9728c7c5a53ac993a9ba233ab45435fa05114a85bcca2be038305c1346aa8","nasal":"4d7d1c4d8ced0a66b6a60e7cd2d62c31d32fa1b708ce622e673e89314081bbeb"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-38-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":38,"verse":9,"english":"And darkened by the gloom, all sides became bewildered. And the entire earth with her mountains, forests, and wocds, trembled.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.604,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-39-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4038009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"55d6edadadf6e6cd6675ed5c8a90088525db4d3bb90804f70c32b95c89aeeb1e","compact":"c55332382e8697fac311ed7493c2b2e8304a37c47ff6a9b6f6d8c6d81bbdfa0c","nasal":"c55332382e8697fac311ed7493c2b2e8304a37c47ff6a9b6f6d8c6d81bbdfa0c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-38-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":38,"verse":10,"english":"Then the whole ground was covered with innumerable monkeys gifted with great strength, and having sharp teeth, and resembling kings of men.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-39-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4038010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8c45f4446e58657c70605b3a740fa19c663bea20d4ca06f977ab47b3c7d9d66e","compact":"226b559e59080958c993d8c5bd0997063670a72e72b0c04f9b94a246738abac6","nasal":"c00d5cd82c47c1da4a7ef1b5e95dae1fcb9c160ab8f41b56153d307f0c60de9d"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-38-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":38,"verse":11,"english":"Then surrounded by leaders of monkey-herds, and retinues numbering hundreds of koțis, and monkey chiefs from rivers, and mountains, and seas, endowed with prodigious strength, and other apes inhabiting forests, having voices resembling clouds-and monkeys hued like the infant sun, or white like the moon, or coloured like the filaments of the lotus, or pale, having their homes in the Golden mountain-in all, numbering ten thousand koțis,-appeared the graceful and heroic monkey, named Satavali.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.643,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-39-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4038011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a26d0aec58ed103d12c42cc7447c45019c9c9b45ce6724dfe2f60512900df7f6","compact":"9aea79f53557e4a2d9301b43eb8b6c93333a8c1c74fcb53b9e7fbb575e386f36","nasal":"acf07f38b125aa9ff47d42beab36fff2ca49457699f53c5b935fa1f45fa190cb"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-38-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":38,"verse":12,"english":"Then surrounded by leaders of monkey-herds, and retinues numbering hundreds of koțis, and monkey chiefs from rivers, and mountains, and seas, endowed with prodigious strength, and other apes inhabiting forests, having voices resembling clouds-and monkeys hued like the infant sun, or white like the moon, or coloured like the filaments of the lotus, or pale, having their homes in the Golden mountain-in all, numbering ten thousand koțis,-appeared the graceful and heroic monkey, named Satavali.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.552,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-39-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4038012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"221cb3ecb899c33f229cdf8ab2d67836af13010fce5e40e1b6483ea0b7fefcae","compact":"8b752fae828e52630beeaa47efafc1016e04d69319f10bd1feb26c56deeba227","nasal":"8b752fae828e52630beeaa47efafc1016e04d69319f10bd1feb2