:"Then appeared to the view the stout monkey, named Durmukha, heroic lord of herds, surrounded by two koțis.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.734,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-39-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4038029","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"515134a82ad002299e15005ef4666c49370f9fd622db75247c7596acac2cb2cc","compact":"3b1784462342d4c3ec4e4ecdd85ac60673974fb523d649dfb7738db3310b3d06","nasal":"3b1784462342d4c3ec4e4ecdd85ac60673974fb523d649dfb7738db3310b3d06"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-38-30","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":38,"verse":30,"english":"And Hanumān showed himself, surrounded by a thousand koțis of monkeys, resembling peaks of Kailāsa, of dreadful vigour.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-39-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4038030","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a1c1130369c7d29f35d062c9b47cf87e95c010c37a9deace17310e84dc497001","compact":"4b2b7a1f2236b94de6bb3f16fd89d429a0137b3aaee41d59d1a482c6f0c9e42e","nasal":"4b2b7a1f2236b94de6bb3f16fd89d429a0137b3aaee41d59d1a482c6f0c9e42e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-38-31","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":38,"verse":31,"english":"And the exceedingly energetic Nala came, attended with an hundred kotis, a thousand, and an hundred monkeys, living in trees.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.707,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-39-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4038031","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cfda943765201147a491988fa3b20b161366769f4dfcd9827412844b04a74e67","compact":"3b09c96d23513946d6b2551a2fde2fe3fba50917e42bde667eea213bee2ed039","nasal":"3b09c96d23513946d6b2551a2fde2fe3fba50917e42bde667eea213bee2ed039"}},{"id":"VR